	chapter_group.639C8B4E3836D569.title: "Cobblemods"
	chapter.6C4349CF7827A5B8.title: "Genetics 101"
	chapter.6C4349CF7827A5B8.chapter_subtitle: ["Every Pokémon is genetically unique"]
	quest.06B1CD143EBBDF22.title: "The Genetic Analyzer"
	quest.06B1CD143EBBDF22.quest_subtitle: "Your window into Pokémon biology"
	quest.06B1CD143EBBDF22.quest_desc: ["Craft a &bGenetic Analyzer&r (iron, glass, redstone and a Poké Ball - check JEI)." "" "&eRight-click&r any Pokémon in the world with it - wild or yours - or use it in the air to pick a Pokémon from your party." "" "The report reads like a Pokédex: every gene comes with a note on what it means for &othat&r Pokémon, and the right side shows its &6Breeding value&r and your best of its species so far. Lost? Press &b? Guide&r."]
	quest.56ED2CE7E35621C1.title: "First Sample"
	quest.56ED2CE7E35621C1.quest_subtitle: "Analyse a Pokémon"
	quest.56ED2CE7E35621C1.quest_desc: ["Every Pokémon now carries its own &dgenetic profile&r, rolled when it was born." "" "The first thing you can read is its &6Genetic Potential&r, graded &aS&r, &aA&r, &eB&r, &eC&r or &cD&r. Wild Pokémon with high potential are born with better minimum stats (IVs), and keep improving as you train them."]
	quest.642477C5A394EAFA.title: "No Two Alike"
	quest.642477C5A394EAFA.quest_subtitle: "Analyse three different Pokémon"
	quest.642477C5A394EAFA.quest_desc: ["Analyse a few Pokémon of the &osame species&r and compare them: their genes differ." "" "Greyed-out rows show what higher &bGenetic Research&r levels will reveal. Research rises as you study more Pokémon, or with &bAnalyzer Upgrades&r (use the one this quest gives you)."]
	quest.07A4E4049F91EDDA.title: "Born for Greatness"
	quest.07A4E4049F91EDDA.quest_subtitle: "Find above-average Genetic Potential"
	quest.07A4E4049F91EDDA.quest_desc: ["Find a Pokémon with &6Genetic Potential 70+&r (grade A or S)." "" "Tip: potential is partly inherited. Two high-potential parents tend to have high-potential offspring."]
	quest.7BF8CEA614B0EBD2.title: "For the Archive"
	quest.7BF8CEA614B0EBD2.quest_subtitle: "Record a genetic profile"
	quest.7BF8CEA614B0EBD2.quest_desc: ["Press &bRecord Profile&r on the Analyzer screen of one of &oyour&r Pokémon. It writes the analysis onto a &bGenetic Record&r, using one paper." "" "Records are handy to compare parents before breeding."]
	quest.5674030B43AE134C.title: "Research Level 2"
	quest.5674030B43AE134C.quest_subtitle: "Stability & Affinity"
	quest.5674030B43AE134C.quest_desc: ["At level 2 the Analyzer shows:" "&b- Genetic Stability&r: how resistant the genome is to change. Low stability means more mutations, and more of them harmful." "&b- Elemental Affinity&r: a hidden leaning towards a type, with a strength grade. Matching the Pokémon's own type, it &aresonates&r (extra EXP). In breeding, strong affinities mean bigger bonuses and bigger risks." "&b- Breeding value&r: one grade for how good the Pokémon is to breed from." "" "Your reward opens the next chapters: &aHeredity&r and &dMutations&r."]
	quest.3F1A6C2E9B7D4058.title: "Growing Pains"
	quest.3F1A6C2E9B7D4058.quest_subtitle: "Train up some potential"
	quest.3F1A6C2E9B7D4058.quest_desc: ["Level up a Pokémon with good &6Genetic Potential&r until one of its IVs rises." "" "Each level up has a chance to raise its &olowest&r IV by 1, up to a ceiling set by its potential: about 17 at grade C, 31 at grade S. The Analyzer shows the ceiling under Genetic Potential."]
	quest.58C4E1B7A2D93F60.title: "In Tune"
	quest.58C4E1B7A2D93F60.quest_subtitle: "Find a resonating affinity"
	quest.58C4E1B7A2D93F60.quest_desc: ["At research level 2, analyse a Pokémon whose &bElemental Affinity&r is one of its own types." "" "It &aresonates&r: it gains extra EXP, more the stronger its affinity grade (up to +15% at S). The note under Elemental Affinity tells you when it does."]
	chapter.2C88263FACF30DC2.title: "Heredity"
	chapter.2C88263FACF30DC2.chapter_subtitle: ["How genes pass from parents to offspring"]
	quest.15C95900440E45BD.title: "The Genetic Incubator"
	quest.15C95900440E45BD.quest_subtitle: "Breeding, CobbleGenetics style"
	quest.15C95900440E45BD.quest_desc: ["Place the &bGenetic Incubator&r, right-click it and pick two party Pokémon (level 15+). Then right-click it with a &aberry&r for each of them: love hearts, and breeding begins." "" "Same family: main-game rules (a shared &eegg group&r and opposite genders, or &dDitto&r). Two &ddifferent&r families make a &dfusion baby&r if Fusionmon is installed!" "" "After a few minutes they come back to your party and an &aEgg&r waits inside: right-click to take it, or leave it for a &aDay Care Aide&r."]
	quest.4C3CACB8E8D2B19A.title: "New Generation"
	quest.4C3CACB8E8D2B19A.quest_subtitle: "Breed two Pokémon"
	quest.4C3CACB8E8D2B19A.quest_desc: ["Keep the &aPokémon Egg&r in your inventory and &ewalk&r: it hatches into a level 1 Pokémon. Its tooltip hints how close it is, and a party Pokémon with &6Flame Body&r or &6Magma Armor&r halves the walk." "" "No time to walk? A &aDay Care Aide&r can hatch it in the Incubator for you (see the Day Care quest)." "" "Its genes are &oa mix&r of both parents plus some randomness - never a copy of either. Three of its stats (IVs) also come from a random parent."]
	quest.2E3352B9C0D17B99.title: "Proud Parent"
	quest.2E3352B9C0D17B99.quest_subtitle: "Analyse one of the parents"
	quest.2E3352B9C0D17B99.quest_desc: ["Analyse one of the parents again and keep its numbers in mind (or &bRecord&r it)."]
	quest.7DB8930071B094AE.title: "Family Resemblance"
	quest.7DB8930071B094AE.quest_subtitle: "Analyse the offspring"
	quest.7DB8930071B094AE.quest_desc: ["Now analyse the offspring. Its potential and stability sit between its parents', and its &bOrigin&r shows its generation." "" "Use the &bHeredity Module&r to reach research level 3 and see &dInherited Traits&r."]
	quest.623898E7FF8509CB.title: "It Runs in the Family"
	quest.623898E7FF8509CB.quest_subtitle: "Identify an inherited trait"
	quest.623898E7FF8509CB.quest_desc: ["At research level 3, analyse a bred Pokémon and read its &dInherited Traits&r." "" "Each trait has two copies (alleles), one from each parent. A &orecessive&r allele only shows when a Pokémon carries two copies - so rare traits can hide for generations and reappear."]
	quest.129462637227545C.title: "Skipped a Generation"
	quest.129462637227545C.quest_subtitle: "Breed out a rare recessive trait"
	quest.129462637227545C.quest_desc: ["Breed an offspring that expresses a &6rare recessive&r trait (highlighted in gold), such as &eShadowproof&r or &eLustrous&r." "" "Tip: at research level 4 the Analyzer shows the hidden allele pairs, and analysing two Pokémon one after the other predicts what their offspring could get."]
	quest.2530A0BFCA34A198.title: "Research Level 3"
	quest.2530A0BFCA34A198.quest_subtitle: "Heredity"
	quest.2530A0BFCA34A198.quest_desc: ["Level 3 adds &bMutation Susceptibility&r, size genes and inherited traits." "" "Your next step: the &5Shadow Research&r chapter."]
	quest.4E8B2D6F1C9A3075.title: "Day Care"
	quest.4E8B2D6F1C9A3075.quest_subtitle: "Let a Day Care Aide hatch an Egg"
	quest.4E8B2D6F1C9A3075.quest_desc: ["An unemployed villager near a &bGenetic Incubator&r takes the &aDay Care Aide&r job (look for the apron)." "" "Leave an Egg in the Incubator: while the aide is close by, &a♥ Day Care&r and its progress float above it, the Egg wobbles more as hatching nears, and the baby goes straight to your party or PC." "" "Click the Incubator for the time left; sneak-click takes the Egg."]
	quest.7C1E5A9D3B2F6048.title: "Prize Bloodline"
	quest.7C1E5A9D3B2F6048.quest_subtitle: "Breed a grade A Pokémon"
	quest.7C1E5A9D3B2F6048.quest_desc: ["Analyse a Pokémon with a &6Breeding value&r of 75 or more (grade A)." "" "The breeding value sums up how good a Pokémon is to breed from: mostly &6Genetic Potential&r, then &bStability&r. The Analyzer remembers your best of every species, so each generation has a target to beat." "" "Tip: parents with different, compatible affinities give their babies extra potential (hybrid vigour), more so with strong affinity grades."]
	chapter.6A6E624E40E54022.title: "Mutations"
	chapter.6A6E624E40E54022.chapter_subtitle: ["When genes change"]
	quest.1D988EF8565F6C9D.title: "Something Different"
	quest.1D988EF8565F6C9D.quest_subtitle: "Identify a mutated Pokémon"
	quest.1D988EF8565F6C9D.quest_desc: ["Some Pokémon carry &dmutations&r: changes to colour, size, stats, type affinity or abilities." "" "Mutations come in five tiers: &7Common&r, &aUncommon&r, &9Rare&r, &5Epic&r and &6Legendary&r. Look for odd colours, glowing or unusual sizes - then analyse."]
	quest.18740B3B46C00B85.title: "Mad Science"
	quest.18740B3B46C00B85.quest_subtitle: "Induce a mutation"
	quest.18740B3B46C00B85.quest_desc: ["Use a &dMutagen&r on a party Pokémon. It forces a mutation - but costs &cgenetic stability&r, and the result can be harmful." "" "Mutagens are a reliable way to get a mutated Pokémon for breeding experiments."]
	quest.126D2C1A28190D8A.title: "Nature's Experiment"
	quest.126D2C1A28190D8A.quest_subtitle: "Find a natural mutation"
	quest.126D2C1A28190D8A.quest_desc: ["Wild Pokémon sometimes spawn mutated. It is more common for genetically unstable ones, and &edouble during thunderstorms&r - a genetic storm."]
	quest.018B70E251DEA7B8.title: "Passed Down"
	quest.018B70E251DEA7B8.quest_subtitle: "Get an inherited mutation"
	quest.018B70E251DEA7B8.quest_desc: ["Breed a mutated Pokémon and analyse its offspring until one inherits the mutation." "" "Parents pass their mutations on directly only sometimes; otherwise the offspring may carry them &olatent&r (hidden). Two carriers can produce one that expresses it again."]
	quest.0C5BB94CFA5F829B.title: "Rare Specimen"
	quest.0C5BB94CFA5F829B.quest_subtitle: "A Rare-tier mutation or better"
	quest.0C5BB94CFA5F829B.quest_desc: ["Find or create a mutation of &9Rare&r tier or higher. Unstable genomes roll higher tiers more often."]
	quest.22B71D651BED3F6E.title: "Research Level 4"
	quest.22B71D651BED3F6E.quest_subtitle: "Mutation Science"
	quest.22B71D651BED3F6E.quest_desc: ["Level 4 shows each mutation's category, origin and exact effects, the hidden allele pairs, latent mutations, and &bbreeding predictions&r: analyse two Pokémon one after the other to see what their offspring could inherit."]
	chapter.69BD8C82EC8F98AC.title: "Advanced Mutation Research"
	chapter.69BD8C82EC8F98AC.chapter_subtitle: ["Instability, environments and rare tiers"]
	quest.180A44BD17520161.title: "Under the Microscope"
	quest.180A44BD17520161.quest_subtitle: "Study a mutation in detail"
	quest.180A44BD17520161.quest_desc: ["At research level 4, analyse a mutated Pokémon and read the full effect list of its mutation."]
	quest.3AD790CA5A9FA3E0.title: "Unstable Genome"
	quest.3AD790CA5A9FA3E0.quest_subtitle: "Find low genetic stability"
	quest.3AD790CA5A9FA3E0.quest_desc: ["Analyse a Pokémon whose effective stability is below 35." "" "Mutagens, negative mutations and &5Shadow corruption&r all erode stability. Unstable Pokémon mutate more - and worse. The &bGene Stabilizer&r repairs corruption damage."]
	quest.72463623FD7A3A44.title: "Shaped by the Land"
	quest.72463623FD7A3A44.quest_subtitle: "An environmental mutation"
	quest.72463623FD7A3A44.quest_desc: ["Some mutations only appear in certain places: deserts and the Nether (&cEmber Heart&r), frozen biomes (&bFrost Adapted&r), the sea (&9Tidal Affinity&r), darkness (&3Bioluminescence&r), storms (&eStorm Charged&r)." "" "Wild Pokémon can spawn with them there, and your party slowly adapts to where you travel."]
	quest.6BA45FA59A8F7A57.title: "Elemental Shift"
	quest.6BA45FA59A8F7A57.quest_subtitle: "An elemental mutation"
	quest.6BA45FA59A8F7A57.quest_desc: ["Elemental mutations change a Pokémon's &dTera Type&r and how it fares in different climates."]
	quest.12F1D7D3E9EEAA35.title: "Hidden Talent"
	quest.12F1D7D3E9EEAA35.quest_subtitle: "An ability mutation"
	quest.12F1D7D3E9EEAA35.quest_desc: ["Ability mutations unlock hidden abilities, speed up friendship, or shield a Pokémon from corruption."]
	quest.2D48DDDB88E6B401.title: "Mutation Catalogue"
	quest.2D48DDDB88E6B401.quest_subtitle: "Discover 10 mutations"
	quest.2D48DDDB88E6B401.quest_desc: ["Analyse Pokémon with 10 different mutations."]
	quest.56BFF9A644C7A8A3.title: "Epic Discovery"
	quest.56BFF9A644C7A8A3.quest_subtitle: "An Epic-tier mutation"
	quest.56BFF9A644C7A8A3.quest_desc: ["Find an &5Epic&r mutation. Some can only be bred: they need other mutations to be present first..."]
	chapter.23DB2B6EF776B2E8.title: "Shadow Research"
	chapter.23DB2B6EF776B2E8.chapter_subtitle: ["Corrupted Pokémon"]
	quest.5244D1F89D102159.title: "A Dark Signal"
	quest.5244D1F89D102159.quest_subtitle: "Shadow Pokémon exist"
	quest.5244D1F89D102159.quest_desc: ["Some Pokémon are &5Shadow Pokémon&r: their hearts are sealed by corruption. They are dark, wrapped in a purple aura, and the most corrupted ones spread darkness around them." "" "They appear rarely in the wild - more at night, much more on a &5new moon&r - and in special places. Use the &5Shadow Beacon&r to call one to you."]
	quest.2A4FAC3AE51D8976.title: "Darkness Stirs"
	quest.2A4FAC3AE51D8976.quest_subtitle: "Encounter a Shadow Pokémon"
	quest.2A4FAC3AE51D8976.quest_desc: ["Battle a wild Shadow Pokémon, or analyse one in the wild."]
	quest.3B8DEA5A1160916C.title: "Snagged"
	quest.3B8DEA5A1160916C.quest_subtitle: "Capture a Shadow Pokémon"
	quest.3B8DEA5A1160916C.quest_desc: ["Shadow Pokémon are harder to catch and arrive with &cno friendship&r. They cannot evolve or breed until purified."]
	quest.088C833226CDAADD.title: "Measuring the Dark"
	quest.088C833226CDAADD.quest_subtitle: "Analyse its corruption"
	quest.088C833226CDAADD.quest_desc: ["The Analyzer shows the &5corruption&r state: Dormant, Unstable, Aggressive, Highly Corrupted or Fully Corrupted." "" "Corruption &cdrains genetic stability&r, and every 20% it reaches leaves lasting damage. The more corrupted, the harder its heart is to reach: friendship grows slowly."]
	quest.7DE4F3B29C90EB15.title: "Purification Supplies"
	quest.7DE4F3B29C90EB15.quest_subtitle: "Prepare to heal"
	quest.7DE4F3B29C90EB15.quest_desc: ["Craft &dPurifying Scents&r: a bottle, a Pecha Berry and a small flower."]
	quest.2DACA2F3819C14CE.title: "First Light"
	quest.2DACA2F3819C14CE.quest_subtitle: "Begin purification"
	quest.2DACA2F3819C14CE.quest_desc: ["Lower your Shadow Pokémon's corruption for the first time: keep it in your party, use a Scent, battle together, or earn its friendship."]
	chapter.6BBDA0EFF43C4727.title: "Purification"
	chapter.6BBDA0EFF43C4727.chapter_subtitle: ["Opening a sealed heart"]
	quest.7531EB337473F853.title: "Open Heart"
	quest.7531EB337473F853.quest_subtitle: "Purify through friendship"
	quest.7531EB337473F853.quest_desc: ["Every point of friendship a Shadow Pokémon gains also wears away its corruption. Walk with it, feed it, care for it."]
	quest.76068254FE5BC041.title: "Battle Bond"
	quest.76068254FE5BC041.quest_subtitle: "Win a battle together"
	quest.76068254FE5BC041.quest_desc: ["Winning battles together purifies. &cLosing deepens the corruption&r."]
	quest.3CDBC350B392DE26.title: "Sanctuary"
	quest.3CDBC350B392DE26.quest_subtitle: "Use a Purification Chamber"
	quest.3CDBC350B392DE26.quest_desc: ["Place a &dPurification Chamber&r and stay near it with your Shadow Pokémon: passive purification is three times faster."]
	quest.0F9BDAF20385F71D.title: "Halfway Home"
	quest.0F9BDAF20385F71D.quest_subtitle: "Corruption 40% or less"
	quest.0F9BDAF20385F71D.quest_desc: ["Bring its corruption down to 40% or less. &dPurification Incense&r is strong, but only works below 60%: it finishes the job, it cannot replace it."]
	quest.36EAFD803A8560EF.title: "Heart Opened"
	quest.36EAFD803A8560EF.quest_subtitle: "Purify a Shadow Pokémon"
	quest.36EAFD803A8560EF.quest_desc: ["At 0% corruption the heart opens: big friendship and stability boosts, half its genetic damage repaired - and sometimes a &6purification-exclusive mutation&r that no breeding can produce."]
	quest.0273CBE416368622.title: "After the Storm"
	quest.0273CBE416368622.quest_subtitle: "Analyse the purified Pokémon"
	quest.0273CBE416368622.quest_desc: ["Compare its genetic profile with what it was as a Shadow Pokémon."]
	quest.442515825CC4B726.title: "Reborn"
	quest.442515825CC4B726.quest_subtitle: "A purification-exclusive mutation"
	quest.442515825CC4B726.quest_desc: ["Purification can awaken &6Purified Aura&r, &5Umbral Resonance&r (only after very deep corruption) or the legendary &6Heartbound&r (only with very high friendship at the moment of purification)."]
	quest.54E1543E8E009E0D.title: "Research Level 5"
	quest.54E1543E8E009E0D.quest_subtitle: "Shadow Analysis"
	quest.54E1543E8E009E0D.quest_desc: ["Level 5 shows exact corruption, resistance, how it was purified, and hints at &6rare genetic combinations&r your Pokémon are close to."]
	chapter.379A25411AEF4966.title: "Advanced Genetic Research"
	chapter.379A25411AEF4966.chapter_subtitle: ["The frontier of Pokémon biology"]
	quest.149B84C8FCF40E76.title: "Genetic Alchemy"
	quest.149B84C8FCF40E76.quest_subtitle: "A rare genetic combination"
	quest.149B84C8FCF40E76.quest_desc: ["Some mutations only appear when others are already present - through breeding or evolution. The research level 5 Analyzer hints when a Pokémon holds some of the factors." "" "Try combining dark pigment with living light..."]
	quest.42B37C20090A37B0.title: "Unbreakable Heart"
	quest.42B37C20090A37B0.quest_subtitle: "Shadow-resistant genetics"
	quest.42B37C20090A37B0.quest_desc: ["Find or breed a Pokémon that resists at least 40% of corruption: the recessive &eShadowproof&r trait, &5Shadow Ward&r or &6Purified Aura&r."]
	quest.6D8525565A8F09CE.title: "Bloodline"
	quest.6D8525565A8F09CE.quest_subtitle: "A third-generation offspring"
	quest.6D8525565A8F09CE.quest_desc: ["Breed the offspring of your offspring's offspring and analyse it."]
	quest.24D77B3D57CA91D5.title: "Heart Healer"
	quest.24D77B3D57CA91D5.quest_subtitle: "Purify five Shadow Pokémon"
	quest.24D77B3D57CA91D5.quest_desc: ["Purify five Shadow Pokémon."]
	quest.5C8A8AE7165E41E9.title: "Living Encyclopedia"
	quest.5C8A8AE7165E41E9.quest_subtitle: "Discover 25 mutations"
	quest.5C8A8AE7165E41E9.quest_desc: ["Analyse Pokémon with 25 different mutations."]
	quest.72A0CA46A6C7E856.title: "Once in a Lifetime"
	quest.72A0CA46A6C7E856.quest_subtitle: "A Legendary-tier mutation"
	quest.72A0CA46A6C7E856.quest_desc: ["The rarest discoveries of all: the bred &6Prismatic Genome&r or the purified &6Heartbound&r."]
